Who we are: 
IRCA Group, an Advent portfolio company, was founded in Italy in 1919, and it is a leading international B2B provider of high-quality semi-finished ingredients such as chocolate, decorations, creams, inclusions, nuts and pistachios, pastry mixes, gelato ingredients, and other essential solutions for industrial clients or other independent artisanal producers.
With more than 2.400 employees, 22 production facilities worldwide, and €1 billion in revenues, IRCA Group has a solid track record of growth and international expansion.

What do we offer: 
• An international and inclusive environment, with opportunities to work on global projects and collaborate with colleagues worldwide
• Career growth opportunities, including possibilities abroad
• Health insurance coverage as per national labor contract
• Company car, mobile phone, laptop

Scope of the Position : Implement the commercial strategy for the German market related to the different segments and the assigned customer portfolio, to achieve the commercial and GM revenue targets. Take care of the relationship with the customer, analyzing the customer and product needs and stimulating new business opportunities. Close collaboration with the different teams like research and development department, pricing, sourcing and supply chain.

Description of Main Activities/Responsibilities:

• Implement the commercial strategy for the channels and customers of competence based on the guidelines received;
• Approach and develop new accounts to grow the region, based on strategic plan revenue/margin.
• Manage the relationship and collaboration with the customer effectively and in line with business objectives;
• Collaborate with other Sales Managers to identify and develop technical and commercial synergies;
• Develop and implement account plans;
• Identify the growth levers of the managed client portfolio;
• Organizing innovation days with the Research and Development team, marketing and chefs;
• Manage sales forecasts and revenue estimates;
• Systematically interact with Research and Development through the provision of clear inputs and direct collaboration in product development, in compliance with company procedures and processes;
• Contributing to product/process innovation processes;
• Carry out reporting and meetings on-site.

Professional and Personal skills:

• Education: Bachelor/master degree. Preferably but not binding, in food science
• Professional Skills: Excellent communication; Strong analytical skills; Ability to plan and achieve goals; Knowledge of the ingredients and, in general, the range of IRCA products; technical knowledge and significant experience gained in product application. Problem solving, entrepreneurship.
• Experiences: 10+ years of technical and commercial experience.
• Language Skills: German and English proficiency.

• Behavioral requirements: commercial aptitude, strong communication, ability to understand customer needs; Can build long-lasting relationships;

Health can’t wait .

Not for symptoms to get worse. Not for a six‑month appointment. Not for a system to catch up. But that’s exactly how healthcare works today. You wait, until you can’t.  Alan exists to end the wait.  Health is a universal right, and we believe this right can only become real when it’s coupled with prevention. We need to stop treating health as something we repair and start treating it as something we build, every day. It’s not solely a question of willpower. It’s the healthcare system itself that needs to work for everyone, in a sustainable way.  So we are building the  new standard in prevention insurance.  Alan is the first company that integrates insurance, prevention, and care into a single, acclaimed user experience.  We are on an incredible journey to build a  global leading company, with a

unique culture

. We already partner with 40K+ companies of all sizes, serving more than 1M+ members, and have reached €800M+ in ARR.  Prevention as the new norm. That's what we're building with our team of 800+ people. If it speaks to you: we're hiring across France, Spain, Belgium, and Canada. And beyond.

⭐️ The Pre-Sales role ⭐️

Our Pre-Sales team strengthens Alan’s Enterprise and Public sector Sales to better handle the specificities of our largest customers.

Here are the main missions of the team you will join:

Master our platform and support Sales team by enabling them with insights, expertise and the relevant tools;

Listen and understand prospects’ needs and work internally on how Alan can address them best;

Build a thorough understanding of the prospect and assess the level of functional alignment with our offering and capabilities;

Participate to RFP submissions and build Alan’s response in collaboration with Sales, Insurance and Product experts;

Join the customer acquisition journey to evangelize our services and products;

Act as voice of the customer feeding Alan’s platform roadmap;

Prepare handover for delightful customers’ onboardings;

Eventually coordinate the most complex customer onboardings leveraging your unique knowledge of the customer’s requirements and specificities.

You will actively participate in developing this growing function within Alan and edit the company to make our Sales teams the most successful of all!  Given the growing need for onsite customer engagement,  this role requires you to be based in Paris or the Île-de-France region  (or within a 2-hour door to door distance with the flexibility to travel to Paris on short notice for customer meetings).  For this opportunity, we are aiming to hire within the D-E

level range  .

⭐️ You will be a great fit if ⭐️

You have  6+ years  of experience working in a SaaS environment, including  at least 3  in a  Pre-Sales / Sales Engineering / Solution Consultant  role.

You are highly experienced in  end-to-end procurement projects  (buyer or supplier side) with involvement in RFI’s, RFQ’s and RFP’s;

